OL,3,CKeeping cool in the heatwave: Why your
OL,4,Cfan might be making you hotter
OL,6,FOn its website, the Department for
OL,7,FEducation suggests that mechanical
OL,8,Ffans should be used to increase air
OL,9,Fmovement if temperatures are below 35C.
OL,11,FFor temperatures above this point,
OL,12,Ffans "may not prevent heat-related
OL,13,Fillness and could worsen dehydration",
OL,14,Fthe department adds.
OL,16,FWhat other methods work to keep cool
OL,17,Finstead?
OL,19,F1. Keep windows and curtains closed
OL,20,Fduring the hottest parts of the day
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G5/12
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
