OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F314A1786688289
OL,3,CKeeping cool in the heatwave: Why your
OL,4,Cfan might be making you hotter
OL,6,FWhile it may seem counterintuitive,
OL,7,Fone of the most effective ways to keep
OL,8,Fyour house cool is to keep windows,
OL,9,Fblinds and curtains closed when the
OL,10,Fsun is strongest.
OL,12,FIf the air outside is hotter than the
OL,13,Fair inside, opening windows can simply
OL,14,Fallow more heat to enter your home.
OL,16,FExperts recommend keeping windows and
OL,17,Fcurtains shut during the day,
OL,18,Fespecially between late morning and
OL,19,Fearly evening when temperatures are at
OL,20,Ftheir highest.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G6/12
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
