PN,31408
SC,0008
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F314A1786688289
OL,3,CKeeping cool in the heatwave: Why your
OL,4,Cfan might be making you hotter
OL,6,FOnce outdoor temperatures begin to
OL,7,Ffall in the evening, it's time to do
OL,8,Fthe opposite.
OL,10,FOpening windows overnight and during
OL,11,Fthe cooler early morning hours allows
OL,12,Fcooler air to circulate through your
OL,13,Fhome and helps remove heat that has
OL,14,Fbuilt up during the day.
OL,16,FCreating a through-draught by opening
OL,17,Fwindows on opposite sides of the house
OL,18,Fcan be particularly effective.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G8/12
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
