OL,3,CKeeping cool in the heatwave: Why your
OL,4,Cfan might be making you hotter
OL,6,FIf it is safe to do so, leaving
OL,7,Fupstairs windows slightly open
OL,8,Fovernight can also help release
OL,9,Ftrapped warm air, as heat naturally
OL,10,Frises.
OL,12,F4. Switch off appliances and
OL,13,Funnecessary electrical items
OL,15,FMany household appliances generate
OL,16,Fheat, even when we do not realise it.
OL,18,FOvens, tumble dryers, dishwashers, and
OL,19,Feven computers and televisions can all
OL,20,Fcontribute to rising indoor
OL,21,Ftemperatures.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G9/12
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
